<title>UK: UK card spending up yr/yr 28.2 pct in Oct -CCRG.</title>
<headline>UK card spending up yr/yr 28.2 pct in Oct -CCRG.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Credit Card Research Group, representing major UK credit and debit card issuers, released the following consumer spending figures for October 1996 -</p>
<p> CARD EXPENDITURE (in mln stg) *   Oct 96    Oct 95   % change</p>
<p> All sectors - total		   7,460     5,818    28.2</p>
<p> Food and drink			  1,873     1,581    18.5</p>
<p> Mixed business			    639	 466    37.0</p>
<p> Clothing				    498	 373    33.5</p>
<p> Household				   637	 495    28.7</p>
<p> Motoring				    932	 760    22.7</p>
<p> Entertainment			     423	 322    31.3</p>
<p> Hotels					299	 231    29.6</p>
<p> Travel					665	 499    33.2</p>
<p> Services				    612	 415    47.4</p>
<p>Credit Card Research Group director Elizabeth Philips said spending on cards was reaching new highs. &quot;During the recession when consumer spending remained stagnant, spending on plastic kept on growing. Now that consumer spending is at its highest level for six years, credit and debit card spending is reaching new highs.&quot;</p>
<p>NOTE * figures adjusted for variations in the number of processing days between months.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
